ig cities  new york uh la san francisco the i the  ideas are not working and this brings us  to crime uh you've got some double-digit  increases in some some significant areas  and there's a feeling among new yorkers  i i feel it as a new yorker and i hear  from other people that the city is not  as safe as it was  you're new to this you just started but  you got a deep background in law  enforcement when are we going to see  details on this safe new york plan and  and what are you expecting to make this  city  livable the way it once was well i'll  say i'm new to this but i'm true to this  okay  you know that i've been doing this for a  while and i was clear on the campaign  trail i said new yorkers it is gangs and  guns every time you see a shooting read  the next sentence gang related so what  did we do yesterday with d.a  eric gonzalez he showed the graph he  brought down three gang crews violent  gang crews and what happened shootings  dropped he brought down a gang crew  yesterday that was known for all of the  violence in certain parts of brooklyn we  have to go after the gangs  everybody agrees you should go after  serious violent crime that's not  controversial but the you know the  manhattan d.a made comments yesterday  about not going after  smaller offenses uh fair beating  resisting arrest there were a couple  that he listed and that's controversial  uh do you think that stopping big crime  begins by going after smaller crime yes  i do but also i know  d.a bragg i i respect him he's a great  prosecutor a former u.s attorney and  here's what i believe in my plan as i  speak with them at the precinct level  someone comes in for a a petty theft  right at the precinct level you identify  that they have a mental health issue  instead of locking them up let's defer  prosecution let's have a local community  based organization that deals with  mental health illnesses handle it right  at the precinct that's the coordination  we need there's no reason to put som